.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-POWER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-power
.Nd the Patina desktop's power menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the menu the power button at the bar's right end opens, after the
clock:
.Bl -tag -width "Shut Down"
.It Lock
Lock the screen at once, with the compositor's
.Ic [lock] command .
.It Log Out
End the session: every app closes, and the login screen comes back.
.It Restart
Restart the computer.
.It Shut Down
Turn the computer off.
.El
.Pp
The last three ask first, in the menu.
What can't be done here is greyed out: Log Out outside a Patina session,
and Restart and Shut Down where the login manager won't allow them.
Escape takes a question back, then closes the menu; so does a click
elsewhere, or running
.Nm
again.
.Pp
Locking and logging out are asked of
.Xr patina-compositor 1
on the session bus; where it can't be asked, Lock runs
.Xr patina-lock 1
itself.
Restarting and shutting down go through logind, or ConsoleKit2 where
there's no logind, which may ask polkit; if they refuse, the menu says
why.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.It Ev PATINA_BAR_EDGE
.Dq top
or
.Dq bottom :
which edge to open from.
.It Ev PATINA_OPEN_AT
Where the bar's button that opened it is, as
.Ql edge,x,y Ns Op ,far
in logical pixels: it opens just past it, centred on it and turned towards
the side of the screen with more room.
Without it, it opens on
.Ev PATINA_BAR_EDGE Ns 's
edge.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
